NEMU default run rootfs overlay summary

Change verified:
- make ARCH=riscv64-nemu run now defaults NEMU_RUN_ROOTFS_OVERLAY to
  Linux/env/logs/linux-front/riscv64-nemu-ubuntu-rootfs/rootfs-overlay.raw
  when the Ubuntu rootfs block image is attached.
- NEMU_RUN_ROOTFS_OVERLAY_RESET defaults to 1 and dry-run output includes
  rm -f for the overlay before NEMU starts.
- The NEMU command line includes both --block=<ubuntu ext4> and
  --block-overlay=<log-dir/rootfs-overlay.raw>.

Verification:
- make -C Linux ARCH=riscv64-nemu -n run PASS, dry-run contains --block,
  --block-overlay, rm -f rootfs-overlay.raw, and [Linux] overlay.
- make -C Linux ARCH=riscv64-nemu paths PASS, prints NEMU_RUN_ROOTFS_OVERLAY
  and NEMU_RUN_ROOTFS_OVERLAY_RESET=1.
- scripts/agent-e2e.sh --profile nemu-ubuntu --task-slug
  nemu-default-run-overlay-e2e PASS.

Boundary:
- This prevents ordinary daily NEMU Ubuntu rootfs run from writing directly to
  the backing ext4 image by default.
- It is still a raw sparse overlay first stage, not qcow2, VM snapshot,
  checkpoint/rollback management, crash-consistency fuzzing, or full QEMU
  block layer.
